# aurora.local / packages/media/pins.env.example
#
# Curated, human-reviewed image pins — the ".example" suffix mirrors the
# existing .env / .env.example convention (see .gitignore): the real
# packages/media/pins.env is gitignored (generated by `scripts/pin.sh
# --refresh`/`--apply`, host-local), so committed curated recommendations
# live here. Copy or merge into packages/media/pins.env to adopt.
#
# See dev/notes/pinnable-versions-progress.md for the full inventory and
# reasoning behind every choice in this file.
#
# Once adopted as pins.env, this is consumed by scripts/lib/render.sh
# render_pins() into the environment before `docker compose up`. It only
# takes effect in compose.yml image: lines after `scripts/pin.sh --apply`
# has rewritten them to ${IMAGE_<SVC>} — that has NOT been run.
# compose.yml is untouched by this work.
#
# Format: repo:tag@sha256:digest.
#
# Digests obtained with:
#   docker buildx imagetools inspect --format '{{.Manifest.Digest}}' <ref>
#
# GENERAL NOTE ON THE *ARR STACK'S RECENCY: LinuxServer.io ships one
# genuinely stable release channel (not `develop-*`/`nightly-*`, which
# are pre-release by name) but that channel still updates roughly weekly,
# following upstream. At the time of this check every current LSIO stable
# tag below is younger than the ~2 week caution bar this task otherwise
# applies — there is no older "stable" tag being served; going further
# back means an EOL/superseded release, not a safer one. Recorded as-is,
# flagged per image, rather than picking an arbitrarily older tag to
# satisfy the rule on paper.

# sonarr — stable tag 4.0.19 (== 4.0.19.2979-ls321), pushed 8 days before
# this check (2026-08-15) — under the fortnight bar, see general note
# above. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed.
IMAGE_SONARR=lscr.io/linuxserver/sonarr:4.0.19@sha256:373159ba768e23a3a1c497d9f2b936addf8fd5b1fdce7dd6a14080ac928bfda0

# radarr — stable tag version-6.3.0.10514, pushed 13 days before this
# check — just inside the fortnight bar. Multi-arch: linux/amd64,
# linux/arm64 — confirmed.
IMAGE_RADARR=lscr.io/linuxserver/radarr:version-6.3.0.10514@sha256:a45b5ab0f850f39edb4cc9c95bbd967b52ddc3d4574a4dfb45561177db6c88f4

# prowlarr — stable tag version-2.5.2.5491, pushed 10 days before this
# check. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed.
IMAGE_PROWLARR=lscr.io/linuxserver/prowlarr:version-2.5.2.5491@sha256:1295cff29d10b486c0d8324d1559a552140a5932bf8b3d87e398654414f63f92

# bazarr — stable tag 1.6.0, pushed 4 days before this check — the
# freshest of the stack; worth a specific "give it a week or two" note if
# the owner is cautious about the subtitle-fetch stack breaking. Multi-
# arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed.
IMAGE_BAZARR=lscr.io/linuxserver/bazarr:1.6.0@sha256:b3d44d324399152be4d50775ff639a364c0fa1cfda67f71b1f38264c4d0ca09f

# seerr — ghcr.io/seerr-team/seerr is the actively maintained successor
# to Jellyseerr/Overseerr (the two projects merged; this is not an
# abandoned fork). Stable tag v3.4.1, released 2026-07-30 (~16 days
# before this check, past the fortnight bar). Multi-arch: linux/amd64,
# linux/arm64 — confirmed. Note the container now runs as non-root
# (UID 1000) as of the Seerr rename — worth checking bind-mount
# permissions on data/media/config if migrating from an older Jellyseerr
# volume.
IMAGE_SEERR=ghcr.io/seerr-team/seerr:v3.4.1@sha256:f4768de5f616248d723e05891f3345a1402123775d03bf0890dbfedc0831bda1

# flaresolverr — NOT abandoned, despite some 2026 commentary suggesting a
# slow release cadence: v3.5.0 was released 2026-05-26 (~12 weeks before
# this check, comfortably stable) and `:latest` resolves to the exact
# same digest today. (Two similarly-named repos, FlareSolverr1 and
# FlareSolverr2, were archived by their owner in Dec 2025 — those are
# unrelated forks, not this project; don't confuse them.) Its
# effectiveness against newer Cloudflare challenges is an open question
# per community reports, which is a capability concern, not a pinning
# one. Multi-arch: linux/386, linux/amd64, linux/arm/v7, linux/arm64 —
# confirmed.
IMAGE_FLARESOLVERR=ghcr.io/flaresolverr/flaresolverr:v3.5.0@sha256:139dfee1c6f89249c8d665d1333a42e8ec74ec0a86bc6bb1c8461e10d3a66a47

# rdtclient — actively maintained via Docker Hub, but its GitHub Releases
# page is misleading: it lists v2.0.142 dated 2023, while Docker Hub
# shows 2.0.142 (and a steady run of preceding point releases roughly
# monthly) pushed only 12 days before this check. The maintainer tags
# Docker images directly from CI without always cutting a matching GitHub
# Release — check Docker Hub tags directly for this project, not GitHub
# Releases. 12 days is just under the fortnight bar; there is a growing
# backlog of open GitHub issues as of Aug 2026, which is a maintenance-
# pace concern worth watching even though releases continue. Multi-arch:
# linux/amd64, linux/arm64 — confirmed.
IMAGE_RDTCLIENT=rogerfar/rdtclient:2.0.142@sha256:647db1c0040b1b28bb0e874fd2b58e315c52004c0c27d24e0e0b9be7f6d92469

# qbittorrent — stable tag 5.2.3, pushed 5 days before this check — very
# fresh, see general note above. Multi-arch: linux/amd64, linux/arm64 —
# confirmed.
IMAGE_QBITTORRENT=lscr.io/linuxserver/qbittorrent:5.2.3@sha256:6816d2b144b1eb97665f886e41e18a14d026ba78c9d0953fc68a1211ea819433

# Checked 2026-08-15 for every image in this file.
